# Landing remotes over form actions

On `packages/landing`, prefer **SvelteKit remote functions** (`$lib/remote/*.remote.ts`) with **Zod v4** over classic `export const actions` in `+page.server.ts`.

## Prefer

- `query` / `command` / `form` from `$app/server`
- Zod v4 schemas (`import { z } from 'zod'`) as the Standard Schema
- `form` for multipart / file uploads; `command` for JSON-only mutations; `query` for reads
- Call `locals.services.*()` inside remotes; unwrap with `unwrapAsync` / `invalid` / `error` / `redirect`

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — packages/landing/src/lib/remote/example.remote.ts
import { form, getRequestEvent } from '$app/server';
import { invalid, redirect } from '@sveltejs/kit';
import { z } from 'zod';

export const saveThing = form(
	z.object({
		title: z.string().trim().min(1).max(200),
		file: z.instanceof(File).optional()
	}),
	async (data) => {
		const { locals } = getRequestEvent();
		const result = await locals.services.things().create(data);
		if (result.isErr()) {
			invalid(locals.t(result.error.message));
		}

		redirect(303, `/things/${result.value.id}`);
	}
);
```

```svelte
<!-- ✅ GOOD — spread remote form; use Form.Group like login -->
<form {...saveThing} enctype="multipart/form-data">
	<Form.Group label={t('Title')} inputId="title">
		<Input id="title" {...saveThing.fields.title.as('text')} />
	</Form.Group>
</form>
```

## Avoid

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — new classic form actions for landing mutations
export const actions: Actions = {
	default: async ({ request, locals }) => {
		const form = await request.formData();
		// ...
	}
};
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — new remotes with Valibot (existing valibot remotes can stay until touched)
import * as v from 'valibot';
```

## Notes

- Keep auth gates / cache headers in `+page.server.ts` `load` when needed; put writes in remotes
- Match login/register flush `Form.Group` + `Input` layout for account-style pages
- Do not invent a second validation stack; Zod is the default for new landing remotes
